<%# locals: (event:, roster_link: false) %>
<%#
  Every tag the tally carries, in the order it carries them, so the counted statuses stay the
  model's business alone. `invited` is the one whose label is not its own name: the legend calls
  that tally "no reply".

  An event nobody has been asked about, every place still reserved, draws no tags and says so in
  words instead: four zeros beside the reserved count read as answers that failed to load rather
  than as nobody asked yet. An event with no registrations at all still draws nothing, since "0 on
  the list" is not a fact worth a line.

  Each tag is its icon and number alone, without a badge, in the theme's status colour: yes in
  success, maybe in warning, no in error and no reply in info; reserved, a place nobody has been
  asked about yet, in the page's ink.

  A fact line like the ones above it, led by the people icon. `roster_link` makes "Responses:" a link
  to the event screen with its roster unfolded, for the next-up card; the event screen itself
  leaves it plain, its roster toggle being right below.
%>
<% colours = { "yes" => "text-success", "maybe" => "text-warning", "no" => "text-error", "invited" => "text-info" } %>
<% counts = event.answer_counts %>
<% if counts.except("reserved").values.any?(&:positive?) %>
  <p class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-1 gap-y-1">
    <%= icon :members, class: "size-4 flex-none" %>
    <% if roster_link %>
      <%= link_to "Responses:", group_event_path(event.group, event, responses: "show"), class: "link link-hover mr-2" %>
    <% else %>
      <span class="mr-2">Responses:</span>
    <% end %>

    <% counts.each do |status, count| %>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 mr-2 <%= colours[status] %>">
        <%= icon status, label: (status == "invited" ? "no reply" : status), class: "size-4" %>
        <%= count %>
      </span>
    <% end %>
  </p>
<% else %>
  <% waiting = event.registrations.size %>
  <% if waiting.positive? %>
    <p class="text-card-fact">Nobody asked yet · <%= waiting %> on the list</p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
